      {
        "id": "lem-kauffman-smoothing-operators-for-braid-crossings",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Bracket smoothings of positive and negative braid crossings",
        "deps": [
          "def-elementary-geometric-half-twist",
          "def-oriented-crossing-sign-writhe-and-blackboard-framing",
          "def-kauffman-bracket-smoothing-and-loop-value"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 1,
        "statement": "Let $\\sigma_i$ be the positive geometric Artin braid crossing in a braid rectangle whose parameter increases from bottom to top, with strand $i$ passing below and strand $i+1$ passing above. Use the bracket chart in which the over-strand runs southwest to northeast, the $A$-smoothing joins top to top and bottom to bottom with weight $A$, and the $B$-smoothing joins left to left and right to right with weight $A^{-1}$. Let $I$ be the through pairing and let $e_i$ be the pairing with a top cap and a bottom cup at positions $i,i+1$. Then the positive crossing has bracket operator $A I+A^{-1}e_i$, and the negative crossing has bracket operator $A^{-1}I+A e_i$.\n\n```tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.82, line cap=round, line join=round]\n  \\begin{scope}\n    \\draw[thick] (-0.55,-1)--(-0.55,1);\n    \\draw[thick] (0.55,-1)--(0.55,1);\n    \\node at (0,1.35) {$I$};\n  \\end{scope}\n  \\begin{scope}[xshift=2.6cm]\n    \\draw[thick] (-0.55,1) .. controls (0.25,0.55) and (0.25,-0.55) .. (0.55,-1);\n    \\draw[thick] (0.55,1) .. controls (-0.25,0.55) and (-0.25,-0.55) .. (-0.55,-1);\n    \\node at (0,1.35) {$e_i$};\n  \\end{scope}\n  \\node at (1.25,0) {$\\sigma_i=A I+A^{-1}e_i$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n```",
        "strategy": "Calibrates the positive half twist against the determinant sign and identifies the two source-chart smoothings with the through and cup-cap pairings; reflection exchanges the two pairings and coefficients.",
