        "statement": "Let $F\\subset S^3$ be a compact connected smoothly embedded surface with nonempty boundary $L$, supplied with a finite disk-and-band presentation. The surface may be nonorientable. A normal transfer $\\tau c$ of an oriented rational multicurve $c$ in the interior of $F$ is its total inverse image in the boundary of a sufficiently small normal interval neighborhood of $F$, oriented by projection onto $c$. Suppose a quadratic form $q$ on $H_1(F;\\mathbb Q)$ is positive definite or negative definite and satisfies $q([c])=\\operatorname{lk}(c,\\tau c)$ for every such rational multicurve. Then $L$ is nonsplit. Definiteness on the zero vector space is allowed.",
