        "statement": "Assume full AC. Any two connected reduced alternating diagrams on the oriented projection sphere that represent the same oriented link type are related by a finite sequence of sphere planar isotopies and flypes. Composite links are included; the diagrams are required to be connected, and a plane drawing is interpreted as a punctured projection sphere.",
        "strategy": "The registered route is Menasco crossing-ball position, incompressible Conway spheres and standard-position alternating tangles, followed by the Menasco–Thistlethwaite geometric flyping reduction with an explicit decreasing complexity; graph matroid exchange alone is insufficient because it can encode mutation.",
